#. type: Title =
#: pages/policy/guiding-policy.adoc:3
#, no-wrap
msgid "Guiding Policy"
msgstr "Vägledande policy"

#. type: Plain text
#: pages/policy/guiding-policy.adoc:6
#| msgid ""
#| "This guiding policy represents the way the Fedora Council would like the "
#| "Project to make its mission a reality."
msgid ""
"This guiding policy represents the way the {team_name} would like the "
"Project to make its mission a reality."
msgstr ""
"Denna vägledande policy beskriver hur {team_name} vill att projektet ska "
"förverkliga sitt uppdrag."

#. type: Plain text
#: pages/policy/guiding-policy.adoc:8
msgid ""
"The Fedora Project's https://docs.fedoraproject.org/en-"
"US/project/#_our_mission[Vision] is:"
msgstr ""
"Fedoraprojektets https://docs.fedoraproject.org/en-"
"US/project/#_our_mission[Vision] är:"

#. type: delimited block _
#: pages/policy/guiding-policy.adoc:11
#| msgid ""
#| "_The Fedora Project envisions a world where everyone benefits from free and "
#| "open source software built by inclusive, welcoming, and open-minded "
#| "communities._"
msgid ""
"_The Fedora Project envisions a world where everyone benefits from free and "
"open source software built by inclusive, welcoming, and open-minded "
"communities_."
msgstr ""
"_Fedoraprojektet ser en värld där alla drar nytta av fri programvara med "
"öppen källkod, skapad av inkluderande, välkomnande och öppensinnade "
"gemenskaper_."

#. type: Plain text
#: pages/policy/guiding-policy.adoc:14
msgid ""
"To accomplish this, our https://docs.fedoraproject.org/en-"
"US/project/#_our_mission[Mission] is:"
msgstr ""
"För att uppnå detta är vårt https://docs.fedoraproject.org/en-"
"US/project/#_our_mission[uppdrag]:"

#. type: delimited block _
#: pages/policy/guiding-policy.adoc:17
#| msgid ""
#| "_Fedora creates an innovative platform for hardware, clouds, and containers "
#| "that enables software developers and community members to build tailored "
#| "solutions for their users._"
msgid ""
"_Fedora creates an innovative platform for hardware, clouds, and containers "
"that enables software developers and community members to build tailored "
"solutions for their users_."
msgstr ""
"_Fedora skapar en innovativ plattform för hårdvara, moln och behållare som "
"gör det möjligt för programutvecklare och gemenskapsmedlemmar att skapa "
"skräddarsydda lösningar för sina användare_."

#. type: Plain text
#: pages/policy/guiding-policy.adoc:20
#| msgid ""
#| "We do this within the context of the four foundations: freedom, friends, "
#| "features, and first."
msgid ""
"We do this within the context of the Four Foundations: Freedom, Friends, "
"Features, and First."
msgstr ""
"Vi gör detta utifrån de fyra grundpelarna: Freedom, Friends, Features och "
"First."

#. type: Title ==
#: pages/policy/guiding-policy.adoc:23
#, no-wrap
msgid "Context"
msgstr "Sammanhang"

#. type: Plain text
#: pages/policy/guiding-policy.adoc:29
#| msgid ""
#| "The Fedora Council identifies the short-, medium-, and long-term goals "
#| "necessary to keep the Project on the leading edge of technology.  The "
#| "Fedora.next initiative focused the outputs of the project around use cases."
#| "  In 2017, we updated the mission statement to reflect changes in the "
#| "computing landscape.  Today, it’s too difficult to build new solutions in "
#| "Fedora."
msgid ""
"The {team_name} identifies the short-, medium-, and long-term goals "
"necessary to keep the Project on the leading edge of technology.  The "
"Fedora.next initiative focused the outputs of the project around use cases."
"  In 2017, we updated the mission statement to reflect changes in the "
"computing landscape.  Today, it is too difficult to build new solutions in "
"Fedora."
msgstr ""
"{team_name} identifierar de kort-, medel- och långsiktiga mål som behövs för"
" att hålla projektet i teknikens framkant. Initiativet Fedora.next "
"fokuserade projektets resultat kring användningsfall. År 2017 uppdaterade vi"
" uppdragsbeskrivningen för att avspegla förändringar i datorlandskapet. I "
"dag är det för svårt att bygga nya lösningar i Fedora."

#. type: Title ==
#: pages/policy/guiding-policy.adoc:32
#, no-wrap
msgid "Our Approach"
msgstr "Vårt tillvägagångssätt"

#. type: Plain text
#: pages/policy/guiding-policy.adoc:37
msgid ""
"We will make it easy for the community to build solutions, address specific "
"developer problems, and meet their end users’ specific needs.  We will do "
"this by encouraging and helping Objectives which make the necessary changes "
"required to ease the process.  This accelerates the transformation of Fedora"
" into a community that enables the construction of solutions."
msgstr ""
"Vi kommer göra det lätt för gemenskapen att bygga lösningar, åtgärda "
"specifika problem för utvecklare och möta deras slutanvändares specifika "
"behov. Vi kommer göra detta genom att uppmuntra och hjälpa olika syften som "
"kommer göra de nödvändiga ändringarna för att förenkla processen. Detta "
"accelererar transformationen av Fedora till en gemenskap som möjliggör "
"konstruktionen av lösningar."

#. type: Plain text
#: pages/policy/guiding-policy.adoc:41
msgid ""
"Internally, Fedora focuses on enabling these solutions to be built.  The "
"outputs of Fedora are the Solutions our community members build.  Our focus "
"on enablement allows experimentation without prior judgement or gate-"
"keeping."
msgstr ""
"Internt fokuserar Fedora på att göra det möjligt att bygga dessa lösningar. "
"Resultaten från Fedora är lösningarna vår gemenskaps medlemmar bygger. Vårt "
"fokus är på att göra det möjligt tillåter experimenterande utan föregående "
"bedömning eller vakhållande."

#. type: Title ==
#: pages/policy/guiding-policy.adoc:44
#, no-wrap
msgid "What does this mean?"
msgstr "Vad betyder detta?"

#. type: Plain text
#: pages/policy/guiding-policy.adoc:48
#| msgid ""
#| "Teams such as Design, Documentation, Packagers, Release Engineering, and "
#| "Quality Assurance provide building blocks and offer services to other "
#| "community members and Teams.  Services and building blocks include: CI "
#| "infrastructure, community building advice and guidance, event funding, logo "
#| "services, RPM or other software packages, swag, testing and validation, user"
#| " support, or UX design."
msgid ""
"Teams such as Design, Documentation, Packagers, Release Engineering, and "
"Quality Assurance provide building blocks and offer services to other "
"community members and Teams.  Services and building blocks include the "
"following:"
msgstr ""
"Grupper som Design, Documentation, Packagers, Release Engineering och "
"Quality Assurance tillhandahåller byggstenar och erbjuder tjänster till "
"andra gemenskapsmedlemmar och grupper. Tjänster och byggstenar omfattar "
"följande:"

#. type: Plain text
#: pages/policy/guiding-policy.adoc:50
msgid "CI infrastructure"
msgstr "CI-infrastruktur"

#. type: Plain text
#: pages/policy/guiding-policy.adoc:51
msgid "Community building advice and guidance"
msgstr "Råd och vägledning för gemenskapsbyggande"

#. type: Plain text
#: pages/policy/guiding-policy.adoc:52
msgid "Event funding"
msgstr "Finansiering av evenemang"

#. type: Plain text
#: pages/policy/guiding-policy.adoc:53
msgid "Logo services"
msgstr "Logotyptjänster"

#. type: Plain text
#: pages/policy/guiding-policy.adoc:54
msgid "RPM or other software packages"
msgstr "RPM eller andra programpaket"

#. type: Plain text
#: pages/policy/guiding-policy.adoc:55
msgid "Swag"
msgstr "Profilmaterial"

#. type: Plain text
#: pages/policy/guiding-policy.adoc:56
msgid "Testing and validation"
msgstr "Testning och validering"

#. type: Plain text
#: pages/policy/guiding-policy.adoc:57
msgid "User support"
msgstr "Användarstöd"

#. type: Plain text
#: pages/policy/guiding-policy.adoc:58
msgid "UX design"
msgstr "UX-design"

#. type: Plain text
#: pages/policy/guiding-policy.adoc:63
#| msgid ""
#| "Anyone may use Building Blocks like software packages and artwork to create "
#| "a Solution.  Example solutions include: Fedora Workstation, KDE Plasma, and "
#| "the Python Classroom Lab.  Teams define criteria for services they provide "
#| "to solution-builders.  For example, teams providing press and promotional "
#| "support may choose to provide additional support to Solutions with larger "
#| "user bases."
msgid ""
"Anyone may use building blocks like software packages and artwork to create "
"a Solution.  Example solutions include: Fedora Workstation, KDE Plasma, and "
"the Python Classroom Lab.  Teams define criteria for services they provide "
"to solution-builders.  For example, teams providing press and promotional "
"support may choose to provide additional support to Solutions with larger "
"user bases."
msgstr ""
"Alla kan använda byggstenar som programpaket och illustrationer för att "
"skapa en lösning. Exempel på lösningar är: Fedora Workstation, KDE Plasma "
"och Python Classroom Lab. Grupper definierar kriterier för de tjänster de "
"ger till lösningsskapare. Grupper som erbjuder press- och "
"marknadsföringsstöd kan till exempel välja att ge ytterligare stöd till "
"lösningar med större användarbaser."

#. type: Plain text
#: pages/policy/guiding-policy.adoc:67
msgid ""
"Teams are free to define elements of their Solutions, such as intent, "
"deliverables, and release cadence.  Teams can build Solutions from any "
"building block and pick and choose what tools they use.  Based on their "
"choices, they get different levels of ability to use the Fedora trademark "
"(i.e. “Fedora Remix” vs “Powered by” vs “Fedora”).  Some solutions are the "
"premier showcases that we call Editions; these are used in the gating tests "
"for our releases."
msgstr ""
"Det står grupper fritt att definiera element i deras lösningar, såsom "
"avsikt, leverabler och utgåvefrekvens. Grupper kan bygga lösningar från "
"godtyckliga byggstenar och välja ut de verktyg de använder. Baserat på deras"
" val får de olika nivåer av möjligheter att använda varumärket Fedora "
"(d.v.s. ”Fedora Remox” gentemot ”Powered by” gentemot ”Fedora”). Några "
"lösningar är de primära exemplen som vi kommer kalla editioner; dessa "
"användes i vakttesterna för våra utgåvor."
